\subsection{The baseline endpoint}

The complete baseline finite inequalities give the conservative raw endpoint
\begin{equation}
 R_{\rm base}=
 \frac{1345575129530003739571681432301188857312754737}
      {685738127494661151198444592354557952000000000}.
 \label{eq:base-R}
\end{equation}
Each baseline lower reserve is
\begin{equation}
 B_{\rm base}=
 \frac{2504748318091942808229694219379799307550987}
      {5485905019957289209587556738836463616000000000}.
 \label{eq:base-B}
\end{equation}
One pays the common finite density approximation; the other pays
compilation and smoothing.  These already include all allowances adopted
before the present same-mask refinement.  They gave the former safe
coefficient $c_{\rm base}=1.96131568$ and the positive slack
\begin{equation}
 R_{\rm base}-2B_{\rm base}-c_{\rm base}
 =\frac{2485450886949055352600565107038318521}
       {2742952509978644604793778369418231808000000000}>0.
 \label{eq:base-lower-slack}

With the substitutions just proved, the conservative raw endpoint is
\begin{equation}
 R=R_{\rm base}+\Delta
  =\frac{1345983686820460038728276256001756964104092721}
        {685738127494661151198444592354557952000000000}.
 \label{eq:current-R}
\end{equation}
Each of the two current lower reserves is
\begin{equation}
 B_0=B_{\rm base}+\frac{\Delta}{8}
 =\frac{2913305608548241964824517919947906098888971}
       {5485905019957289209587556738836463616000000000}.
 \label{eq:current-B}
\end{equation}
From \eqref{eq:current-weight-to-count}, the actual lower compilation,
finite induction, signed root insertion and the same-mask refinement,
\begin{equation}
 \liminf_{\substack{N\to\infty\\2\mid N}}
         \frac{D_{1,2}(N)}{H_N}\ge R-2B_0.
 \label{eq:current-lower-derived}
\end{equation}
Here
\begin{equation}
 R-2B_0
 =\frac{5381021441673291912948280506087079950317481913}
       {2742952509978644604793778369418231808000000000},
 \label{eq:current-after-budgets}
\end{equation}
and exact subtraction gives the strict slack
\begin{equation}
 R-2B_0-c
 =\frac{13457260926863633771775678584711245753}
       {2742952509978644604793778369418231808000000000}
       >4.9061\cdot10^{-9}>0.
 \label{eq:current-lower-slack}
\end{equation}
In particular $D_{1,2}(N)\ge cH_N$ eventually, with the new
$c=1.96176252$.
